# E-Commerce Frontend Rules

## Context
Next.js 14 App Router + TypeScript. Deployed on Vercel. Core packages: Zustand (global state),
React Query (server state), Zod (schema validation), Tailwind CSS (styling).

Pages live in app/, shared UI in components/shared/, feature-specific components in
components/features/. Server components are the default — add "use client" only when
browser APIs or interactivity are required.

## Style
- Use TypeScript strict mode — tsconfig.json enforces this.
- Prefer named exports over default exports.
- Use Tailwind utility classes; avoid inline style attributes or CSS modules.
- Components must stay under 200 lines; extract sub-components when they grow.
- Prefer named exports over default exports.
- Write clean, maintainable code throughout the codebase.

## Rules
- NEVER store authentication tokens in localStorage — use httpOnly cookies.
- ALWAYS validate API responses with Zod schemas before consuming data.
- MUST write a unit test for every custom hook (use Vitest + Testing Library).
- Use React Server Components for data fetching when the component has no interactivity.
- Co-locate tests next to the source file (Button.tsx → Button.test.tsx).
- Keep React Query query keys in a central keys.ts file per feature directory.
